# git-stats collection archive, written here by ~/stats/check-augur.sh.
#
# Views, clones, referrers and the stargazer list are owner-only analytics, and
# they include other people's names and email addresses. This repository is
# public, so committing the archive would publish them.
#
# The leading slash is deliberate: an unanchored `data/` would also match a
# demo/data/ or docs/data/ that is meant to be committed.
/data/

# The sandboxed agent workspace built by demo/make-agent-fixtures.py, and the
# recording made from it.
#
# The workspace is generated rather than committed on purpose: it contains a
# CLAUDE.md carrying a smuggled instruction, and `augur agents` walks a tree
# rather than asking git what is in it. Committing the fixture would mean every
# clone of this repository carried a live prompt injection for the next
# person's agent to read.
/demo/workspace/
/demo/augur-showcase.mp4
